{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/908870-alternate-meta-sabbat-play-by-post","id":908870,"title":"Alternate Meta Sabbat Play-By-Post","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-06T21:13:52-07:00","id":908870,"title":"Alternate Meta Sabbat Play-By-Post","content":"As stated, this is a very different meta. The main plot goes as follows:<br /> <br /> In the Dark Ages when the Tremere begin slaughtering the Salubri the Baali, happy to see those with three eyes go, start aiding the Tremere and get buddy buddy with those who had been demonologists at first. The Tremere start spreading word of how these vampires have been much maligned, especially by the Salubri(!), who only want to help stop those vampires who posit true animosity towards the rest of vampire kind. As time goes on the Baali warn the Tremere about Augustus Giovanni's plan, leading to the Tremere to levy a major curse on him (w/demonic help) that makes Cappadocious/Ashur's final drop of blood anathema to the Venetian. Upon Diablerie of Ashur the would be second usurper crumbles to ash, leaving the great soul of Cappadocious to rot in limbo and taking care of one of their biggest rivals in blood magic. But this isn't enough; the Assamite and Tzimisce know too much blood magic themselves and are stepping on Tremere toes.<br /> <br /> Cut to the Carpathians where the Molochim Baali make their home and are allied with the Old Clan and Modern Tzimisce - especially with the Kolduns as they help tap into Kupala's power while making sure the demon never rises. Hearing of their brethren coming with the Tremere to destroy their allies they tap into all the abilities they have while warning the Tzimisce about this. The result is that with Daimonion, Koldunic Sorcery, and heavy secrets rent from tortured demons, the Blood Brothers are made centuries before their time. The Nergali Baali and the Molochim Baali wage war with their respective allies, coming to a stalemate of magic, servants, and taint. For years this is unbroken.<br /> <br /> During the Anarch Revolts that led to the formation of the Camarilla and Sabbat the Nergali Baali play their trump card by triggering the true power behind their curse of the Assamite, causing them to turn on each other ala Week of Nightmares until the head sorcerer of Alamut finally cracks the way to make the curse crave just other vampire blood again instead of their own (for now) and the weakened, flensed Assamites accept the curse of the Tremere if they'd just leave them alone. The Camarilla, when forming, recognizes the allies of the Tremere and all of what the Baali did and accept them into their ranks. The Masquerade goes into heavy effect, white washing all the rumors of 'demons' and what horrendous acts the Nergali Baali did as just lies from Carthage and heavy rumor. Why the Baali are so reviled are lost to time.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, however, doesn't buy this. The Molochim Baali know full well that the Nergali Baali aspire to bring corruption for the sake of power to the world and are eager to make deals with demons instead of wringing the knowledge from them and killing them as is proper. With the formation of the Sabbat they join and immediately found the Inquisition to make sure no demon worship ever happens in the Sabbat. This newfangled conglomeration of vampires even rescues the faltering Salubri and offer them sanctuary against the vile Tremere.<br /> <br /> Current Day: The Camarilla is powerful, as they often have vampires who turn to the demonic to rise in ranks beyond their means and rumors have it that some Nosferatu, Tremere, and Ventrue have even found ways to diablerize demons and capture their powers. How safe this is is up for debate though. The Sabbat has never gone through a Civil War as the Baali, Cappadocians, and Salubri remind those in charge how easy it is to turn on yourself and hammer into people that it is community, even if it is a mercenary style one, that keeps them in order.<br /> <br /> The game will center around an Inquisition Pack (or perhaps just demon hating one) that is fighting for control of Tennessee which the Nergali Baali use as a way to pervert faiths into bigoted, demonic housing gardens for their Embraces.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.myth-weavers.com/forumdisplay.php?f=37496\" target=\"_blank\">Game and Character Creation are here.</a><br /> <br /> If this seems up your alley or you want to play a Baali or Cappadocian in the modern world, give it a spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Debating between ghouls and hunters PbP","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11874-melora","name":"Melora","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}